# Terms no page may use, and what to say instead: `term => say instead`. Checked everywhere on a
# page, code blocks too.
.tar.gz => the Linux portable build is a .tar.xz
agent.run-command => removed, see the code
defwidget@warden => no such widgets.json entry
# In alpha the docs describe only the current release (CLAUDE.md, "Docs for alpha"). These are the
# unambiguous markers of narrated history. "previously", "no longer" and "older" are not denied:
# many of their uses are fine (a limit, the user's own older data), so review catches those.
Warden => removed; the Vault, History, Audit, Jobs and Swarm are panes of their own
Armory => removed; say Connectors or Memory
armory.json => the bundle manifest is bundle.json
Knowledge pane => the pane is Memory
formerly => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
Formerly => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
used to be => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
was renamed => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
renamed from => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
Earlier names => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
# Narrated history by pattern: `/regex/flags => say instead` (a regular expression, matched per line).
# A page that must keep one states why with `allow: term @ path => reason` (path ends the page's path).
/since v?0\.[0-9]/ => in alpha the docs describe only the current release; drop the version
/\bin v?0\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+/ => in alpha the docs describe only the current release; drop the version
/once labell?ed/ => in alpha the docs describe only the current release
Agent App API => retired name; say what the page means now
Stats panel => retired name; say what the page means now
Pre-Launch Auth => retired name; say what the page means now
